  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Thursday)\nIssued at 1147 AM CDT FRI SEP 25 2026\n\nWe had a much cooler start to the day across Central Alabama with\nlow temps in the upper 50s to low 60s this morning. High pressure\nbuilding in will provide several days of pleasant weather across\nthe region. High temps today through the weekend will generally\nrange from the upper 70s to mid 80s with overnight lows dropping\ndown into the mid 50s to low 60s. Increased subsidence and drier\nair will keep us rain-free into early next week. The upper level\npattern begins to change early next week as a weak shortwave cuts\ninto the Tennessee Valley on Monday and Tuesday, followed by a\nstronger upper trough late in the work week. However, limited\nmoisture in place keeps dry conditions in place through mid week.\nLow to medium chances for showers and storms return to the\nforecast late in the week as the aforementioned upper trough and\naccompanying cold front near the region.\n\nA more southerly flow returns by early next week which will\nunfortunately lead to warming temperatures across Central\nAlabama. High temps rebound into the upper 80s to 90 degrees by\nTuesday and look to continue through the work week.\n\n95/Castillo",
